Analytical thinking
.identifying and defining a problem then solving it using data in an organized, step-by-step manner

Aspects to Analytical thinking
.Visualization
    .graphical representation of information 
        .graphs, maps, charts 
    .helps analysts understand and explain information more effectively 
.Strategy
    .know/ picture what to achieve with the data and how to get there 
    .improves the quality and usefulness of the data we collect 
.Problem-orientation
    .identify, describe, and solve the problem
.Correlation
    .identifying the correlation between two or more pieces of data 
    .correlation does not equal causation 
.Detail-oriented thinking/ big-picture thinking
    .zoom out to see possibilities and opportunities 


